        "whyGood": "Exceptional low mileage for a 30-year-old car with a clean accident history. The M30's 3.0L V6 is smooth and proven reliable when maintained. At $7,485 it leaves substantial budget for a pre-purchase inspection and any deferred items.",
        "whatToVerify": "Rubber seals and convertible top mechanism can be costly on 30-year-old cars — have a specialist inspect carefully. Check for frame or underbody rust. Verify cooling system, transmission fluid, and timing belt service history.",
        "bottomLine": "Best value-per-mile on this list. A low-mileage 1991 M30 is a genuine rarity — budget $400 for a thorough pre-buy inspection and enjoy a rare, understated classic."
      },
      {
        "rank": 2,
