        "verified": [],
        "whyGood": "The N54 twin-turbo inline-six is a fan favorite for performance and tuning potential. 48K miles is well within the engine's useful life. One of the most engaging driver's cars in this price bracket.",
        "whatToVerify": "Check high-pressure fuel pump (HPFP) service history — a documented early N54 issue. Listen for wastegate rattle on cold start. Verify timing chain and any walnut-blast service (DI carbon buildup). Look for boost leaks.",
        "bottomLine": "One of the best performance-per-dollar cars on this list. N54 issues are well-documented and fixable; a clean inspection makes this a strong buy for an enthusiast."
      },
